From d071f117f76c3e3b1bd7a2760552b65697494454 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shardul Bankar <shardul.b@mpiricsoftware.com>
Date: Tue, 26 May 2026 04:45:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] mptcp: extend BRF kcov wrap to HMAC failure reset paths

Patch 0002 wrapped the HMAC validation arithmetic inside
subflow_hmac_valid (server-side third-ACK) and subflow_thmac_valid
(client-side SYNACK).  Coverage was captured for the bitwise
compare itself, but the caller-side failure handling -- the MIB
increment and reset-reason assignment that emit MPTCP_RST_EMPTCP
-- ran outside that wrap.

The merged HMAC reset fixes a6da02d4c00f (HMAC EPROHIBIT -> EMPTCP
at server ACK validation) and c4a99a921949 (JOINACKMAC ->
JOINSYNACKMAC at client SynAck) touched exactly these
post-validation code paths.  Coverage feedback on them lets the
BRF harness's MP_JOIN HMAC mutation surface (NFQUEUE-driven HMAC
bit-flip + nonce mutation) confirm not just that the validation
gates were exercised but that the failure reset emission was
reached -- a separate signal that matters for the RST_EMPTCP
per-event MIB counter coverage in the in-flight v3 series
(mptcp_mib_counters task).

Add BRF_MPTCP_KCOV_START / _STOP pairs around the two failure
branches.  Each wrap is two lines of additions in a branch that
only fires when a HMAC mutation matches the kernel's failure
path; zero cost on the success path.  Sequential with the
patch-0002 wraps inside the *_hmac_valid functions (no nesting
-- the inner wrap stops before the function returns false, the
outer wrap starts after).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-4-7
Signed-off-by: Shardul Bankar <shardul.b@mpiricsoftware.com>
---
 net/mptcp/subflow.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/mptcp/subflow.c b/net/mptcp/subflow.c
index ba82c4713c6f6..fed6c16659e5e 100644
--- a/net/mptcp/subflow.c
+++ b/net/mptcp/subflow.c
@@ -589,8 +589,10 @@ static void subflow_finish_connect(struct sock *sk, const struct sk_buff *skb)
 			 subflow->backup);
 
 		if (!subflow_thmac_valid(subflow)) {
+			BRF_MPTCP_KCOV_START(msk);
 			MPTCP_INC_STATS(sock_net(sk), MPTCP_MIB_JOINSYNACKMAC);
 			subflow->reset_reason = MPTCP_RST_EMPTCP;
+			BRF_MPTCP_KCOV_STOP(msk);
 			goto do_reset;
 		}
 
@@ -919,8 +921,10 @@ static struct sock *subflow_syn_recv_sock(const struct sock *sk,
 			}
 
 			if (!subflow_hmac_valid(subflow_req, &mp_opt)) {
+				BRF_MPTCP_KCOV_START(owner);
 				SUBFLOW_REQ_INC_STATS(req, MPTCP_MIB_JOINACKMAC);
 				subflow_add_reset_reason(skb, MPTCP_RST_EMPTCP);
+				BRF_MPTCP_KCOV_STOP(owner);
 				goto dispose_child;
 			}
 
